From 805d3855867dee4a9046d3a79f2f0b1f6a2ac847 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:58:05 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs(commands): fix five more claims the code does not back

- validate.md hard gate demanded "0 errors, 0 warnings". Lint reports 28
  warnings / 0 errors by design (explicit-table-ids and two Convex rules are
  configured warn), so /validate could never exit. Gate on exit 0 and zero
  errors; treat warnings as a named baseline that must not grow.
- validate.md told the agent to run `npm audit`. This repo has only bun.lock,
  so that exits ENOLOCK and invites a stray package-lock.json. Use `bun audit`.
- forge-workflow.md claimed pre-commit blocks source changes without tests.
  lefthook.yml runs lint, type-check and sync:agents --check, nothing else.
  Say what the hooks actually do.
- forge-workflow.md ordered the Docs workflow as verify -> ship. /verify is a
  post-merge check that needs a merged PR, so that order cannot run. It is
  validate -> ship.
- plan.md sent the user to `/plan <slug> --continue` after the proposal PR, but
  the entry gate rejects every non-master branch and would otherwise re-create
  the existing worktree. Handle --continue before the gate and resume in place.
- ship.md's fallback PR body is the only one this repo ever uses (no template
  exists) and had no slot for the demo or acceptance checklist that AGENTS.md
  makes the merge artifact. Added both.

Harness mirrors regenerated with `bun run sync:agents`.

Found by codex review on PR #132.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
